Package: dw9719-ipu3-dkms
Version: 1.4
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, build-essential, sbsigntool, zstd
Maintainer: Matthew Hale <matthew-hale@localhost>
Description: Surface IPU3 camera drivers for the focus motor and rear sensor
 Ubuntu 7.0 dropped the I2C device id table from the dw9719 lens driver.
 The Surface focus motor is a plain I2C device, so the driver never binds.
 That unfinished link blocks every camera, and libcamera lists none.
 .
 This package builds the upstream driver (commit d7fe0d53b2a8, which puts
 the I2C id table back) and installs it ahead of the stock module. It also
 programs the OV8865 rear sensor's mode registers when streaming starts,
 then writes exposure and gain again. Without the mode program, the rear
 camera sends a full-size frame into a smaller buffer, delivers one
 picture, and then stalls. DKMS rebuilds both modules when a new kernel
 is installed. Secure Boot must trust the local module key or the
 modules will not load.
